### Core Architectural Principles
1. **Context as the Boundary Seam**: The React Contexts ([AuthContext.tsx](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/.vscode/Rater/src/context/AuthContext.tsx) and [PostContext.tsx](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/.vscode/Rater/src/context/PostContext.tsx)) are the only entry points that communicate with the mock database layer ([mockData.ts](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/.vscode/Rater/src/logic/mockData.ts)). UI components consume data exclusively via high-level hooks (`useAuth()`, `usePosts()`) and have no knowledge of underlying persistence. This guarantees that migrating to Supabase requires changing only these two context files; your UI components will remain unchanged.
2. **Ephemeral vs. Persistent State**: 
   * **Zustand** is utilized exclusively for ephemeral, high-frequency client-side UI states, such as tracking post swipe sequences ([navigationStore.ts](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/.vscode/Rater/src/store/navigationStore.ts)) for gestures.
   * **React Context** handles heavy, global persistent states (users, sessions, posts) that are backed by the database.
3. **Database-Driven Metrics**: To avoid client-side race conditions and state sync problems when multiple users submit ratings, average scores are generated dynamically in the database using PostgreSQL relational **Views**.

