## 5. Supabase & Cloudinary Media Upload Strategy

In standard production web applications, raw image binary files are never stored inside standard database columns to avoid table bloat and high egress costs. Instead, Rater employs a **hybrid storage pipeline**:
1. **Images** are uploaded directly to **Cloudinary** (CDN/asset storage).
2. **Post metadata** and the optimized **secure Cloudinary image URL** are saved inside the **Supabase Database**.

### Post Creation and Image Upload Sequence

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Designer
    participant FE as Next.js Frontend (PostForm.tsx)
    participant Cloud as Cloudinary API
    participant Supa as Supabase Database

    User->>FE: Selects Image & Enters Metadata
    FE->>FE: 1. Locally validate size (<5MB) and type (PNG/JPG)
    FE->>FE: 2. Set button state to isLoading={true}
    
    %% Cloudinary Upload
    Note over FE,Cloud: Phase 1: Upload Asset to CDN
    FE->>Cloud: 3. POST raw file to Cloudinary Upload endpoint
    Note right of FE: We can use signed uploads or an <br/>unsigned upload preset for client uploads.
    Cloud->>Cloud: Optimize, compress, and host image
    Cloud-->>FE: 4. Returns 200 OK with secure CDN URL <br/> (https://res.cloudinary.com/...)
    
    %% Supabase Save
    Note over FE,Supa: Phase 2: Save Metadata in Database
    FE->>Supa: 5. INSERT INTO posts {title, category, description, image_url: CDN_URL, avatar_id}
    Supa->>Supa: Validate relationships and foreign keys
    Supa-->>FE: 6. Returns 201 Created with saved Post row
    
    FE->>FE: 7. Trigger success screen and play Lottie animation
    FE-->>User: Redirect to Feed
```

