## 7. Realtime Synchronization Setup

To maximize user engagement, we subscribe to database changes directly from the client. When a user is viewing a design under `/post/[id]`, review metrics should update in real-time as other users leave feedback.

### Subscribing to PostgreSQL Changes
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const channel = supabase
    .channel(`live-post-reviews-${postId}`)
    .on(
      'postgres_changes',
      { event: 'INSERT', schema: 'public', table: 'reviews', filter: `post_id=eq.${postId}` },
      (payload) => {
        // Optimistically merge reviews in context or increment review counter
        console.log('Real-time review arrived:', payload.new);
      }
    )
    .subscribe();

  return () => {
    supabase.removeChannel(channel);
  };
}, [postId]);
```

